00:34:06.110 --> 00:34:06.943
And he said,

781
00:34:06.943 --> 00:34:10.080
"There's this great fellowship of human awareness,

782
00:34:10.080 --> 00:34:14.290
and there's not that many people, but when you are one,

783
00:34:14.290 --> 00:34:17.300
you can recognize others and this is the most real thing."

784
00:34:17.300 --> 00:34:20.140
So, he says, "you got to take this seriously."

785
00:34:20.140 --> 00:34:22.130
So I was his student.

786
00:34:22.130 --> 00:34:26.670
And one thing I noticed was, I was having trouble

787
00:34:26.670 --> 00:34:27.503
living up to it.

788
00:34:27.503 --> 00:34:28.990
Because there was drugs and alcohol,

789
00:34:28.990 --> 00:34:31.450
all these distractions and I realized,

790
00:34:31.450 --> 00:34:33.037
if I'm true to this deepest thing that I know,

791
00:34:33.037 --> 00:34:35.480
and I didn't get from my synagogue,

792
00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:36.963
I got it from Jack Bishop.

793
00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:40.330
And I told Jack, I gotta get outta here,

794
00:34:40.330 --> 00:34:42.113
and I gotta go somewhere where,

795
00:34:43.210 --> 00:34:45.260
they're gonna make me be this.

796
00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:46.660
And that's why I joined the Marine Corps.

797
00:34:46.660 --> 00:34:50.280
I joined the Marine Corps because, you know,

798
00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.650
they shave your heads and you can't talk for three months.

799
00:34:52.650 --> 00:34:56.023
I mean, I wanted the eradication of that ego

800
00:34:59.660 --> 00:35:01.770
that I'd built up in high school, downed to nothing

801
00:35:01.770 --> 00:35:02.630
and built up from there.

802
00:35:02.630 --> 00:35:03.463
And that's what the Marines Corps-

803
00:35:03.463 --> 00:35:04.296
And you had this self-awareness...

804
00:35:04.296 --> 00:35:05.306
You had that level of self-awareness

805
00:35:05.306 --> 00:35:06.280
about that at that time-

806
00:35:06.280 --> 00:35:08.500
I'm sitting here thinking to myself when I was 17, 18,

807
00:35:08.500 --> 00:35:12.530
I really can't believe those were my actual thoughts.

808
00:35:12.530 --> 00:35:16.600
I need to eradicate myself and build from the core.

809
00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:17.540
Mm-hmm.

810
00:35:17.540 --> 00:35:18.373
And-

811
00:35:18.373 --> 00:35:22.380
So go into this institution, allow them to break you down,

812
00:35:22.380 --> 00:35:24.470
where you're confronted with yourself

813
00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:28.720
in that very real way and rebuild yourself.

814
00:35:28.720 --> 00:35:30.010
That's what-
Under that kind of,

815
00:35:30.010 --> 00:35:31.870
that level of discipline and rigor.

816
00:35:31.870 --> 00:35:33.324
Yeah. And it did it.

817
00:35:33.324 --> 00:35:35.200
It was true.

818
00:35:35.200 --> 00:35:37.610
It really did it.

819
00:35:37.610 --> 00:35:39.590
And what I discovered was in that, let's say,

820
00:35:39.590 --> 00:35:42.370
100 guys in a platoon, in a basic training platoon,

821
00:35:42.370 --> 00:35:44.520
about 20 where these guys.

822
00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:45.558
Really?

823
00:35:45.558 --> 00:35:46.391
Wow.

824
00:35:46.391 --> 00:35:47.790
There were so many spiritual seekers.

825
00:35:47.790 --> 00:35:49.469
So that was what year?

826
00:35:49.469 --> 00:35:50.302
Yeah, 73.

827
00:35:50.302 --> 00:35:51.480
73.
1973.

828
00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:55.130
Yeah, so my drill instructor was one of them.

829
00:35:55.130 --> 00:35:58.250
You know, a person in the fellowship, I'll say,

830
00:35:58.250 --> 00:35:59.550
for lack of a better term.

831
00:36:00.450 --> 00:36:03.473
So he calls me in, you know,

832
00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:06.793
so the way you get called in was,

833
00:36:07.972 --> 00:36:12.370
they name a class of like football players

834
00:36:12.370 --> 00:36:13.770
or whatever they needed.

835
00:36:13.770 --> 00:36:16.540
So he says, "all Hebrew motherfucker,

836
00:36:16.540 --> 00:36:18.090
report to the duty office."

837
00:36:18.090 --> 00:36:20.557
So we're all looking around, okay, so, count on the door,

838
00:36:20.557 --> 00:36:23.400
"sir, one Hebrew motherfucker reporting as ordered."

839
00:36:23.400 --> 00:36:25.680
So, I go in and he looks at me and he looks at my file

840
00:36:25.680 --> 00:36:27.327
and he sees I have a high IQ, looks he says,

841
00:36:27.327 --> 00:36:28.627
"what are you doing here?"

842
00:36:30.932 --> 00:36:34.610
So I said, "oh, fight for my country."

843
00:36:34.610 --> 00:36:37.210
He goes, "what you're really doing here?"

844
00:36:37.210 --> 00:36:40.920
So I just had to be honest as I need to transform.

845
00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:43.600
I just kind of confessed.

846
00:36:43.600 --> 00:36:44.970
And he says, "okay."

847
00:36:44.970 --> 00:36:46.510
He says, "how many people in the Marine Corps

848
00:36:46.510 --> 00:36:47.910
do you think were like you?"

849
00:36:49.530 --> 00:36:50.693
I said one in 1000.

850
00:36:50.693 --> 00:36:52.750
He said, one in 10,000.

851
00:36:52.750 --> 00:36:55.800
So he says, "don't tell anybody about it,

852
00:36:55.800 --> 00:36:57.630
keep your mouth shut."

853
00:36:57.630 --> 00:36:58.860
He said, "I'll try to help you."

854
00:36:58.860 --> 00:37:00.780
Wow. A little bit of a guardian angel.

855
00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:02.490
Whoa. And-

856
00:37:02.490 --> 00:37:05.930
Because he feared you'd get chewed up and spit out?

857
00:37:05.930 --> 00:37:07.630
Yeah. So he, in a way, I mean,

858
00:37:07.630 --> 00:37:11.160
he was a tough Marine Corps drill Sergeant,

859
00:37:11.160 --> 00:37:14.810
but he had his eye out for me.

860
00:37:14.810 --> 00:37:19.120
And it was crazy because, you know,

861
00:37:19.120 --> 00:37:21.563
okay, so, one thing he did was,

862
00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:24.563
he would play with our minds,

863
00:37:25.560 --> 00:37:27.180
and he wanted to see who got it.

864
00:37:27.180 --> 00:37:30.990
So, one time we're at the chow hall and he says, you know,

865
00:37:30.990 --> 00:37:32.390
we're standing here he says,

866
00:37:33.257 --> 00:37:37.010
"IPT physical trained are platoon to death.

867
00:37:37.010 --> 00:37:40.793
And the ghosts are here as are their ghost rifles.

868
00:37:42.220 --> 00:37:44.610
And I want everybody to pick up your ghost rifle

869
00:37:44.610 --> 00:37:46.320
because you think just 'cause you're outside the chow hall,

870
00:37:46.320 --> 00:37:48.100
you don't have to do close order drill?"

871
00:37:48.100 --> 00:37:50.410
He says, "everybody gets their rifle.

872
00:37:50.410 --> 00:37:51.937
Make sure you have the right rifle."

873
00:37:53.050 --> 00:37:55.280
Like I was looking around, so, I and the 20 other guys

874
00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:57.160
we all start picking up ghost rifles.

875
00:37:57.160 --> 00:37:57.993
So then everybody says,

876
00:37:57.993 --> 00:37:59.560
"okay, so we all pick up our ghost rifles."

877
00:37:59.560 --> 00:38:02.277
He says, "does everybody have the correct rifle?"

878
00:38:03.770 --> 00:38:05.860
I said, this private doesn't sir.

879
00:38:05.860 --> 00:38:08.970
So he goes, "who in the fuck has private Finley's rifle?"

880
00:38:08.970 --> 00:38:10.500
So somebody goes, "sir, this private,

881
00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:11.800
would you please give it to ref?"

882
00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:14.287
So, we're doing all this stuff and the other guys are going,

883
00:38:14.287 --> 00:38:15.780
"what is happening here?"

884
00:38:15.780 --> 00:38:17.500
So he would play mind games with us

885
00:38:17.500 --> 00:38:21.060
the whole way through bootcamp, and I and a few others

886
00:38:21.060 --> 00:38:21.920
got it.

887
00:38:21.920 --> 00:38:23.520
Expand reality.

888
00:38:23.520 --> 00:38:24.530
It's like my teacher in high school,

889
00:38:24.530 --> 00:38:25.780
I went from the high school teacher

890
00:38:25.780 --> 00:38:27.070
to the Marine Corps teacher.

891
00:38:27.070 --> 00:38:28.880
And the whole thing was,

892
00:38:28.880 --> 00:38:31.710
we're living in a world that you don't get, it's a mystery,

893
00:38:31.710 --> 00:38:33.640
open your minds up.

894
00:38:33.640 --> 00:38:34.860
So-
A flip side of that-

895
00:38:34.860 --> 00:38:35.693
Yeah.

896
00:38:35.693 --> 00:38:37.970
Experience would have been for you to,

897
00:38:37.970 --> 00:38:40.710
rather than join the Marine Corps,

898
00:38:40.710 --> 00:38:43.670
to go to India and do the Ram Dass thing, right?

899
00:38:43.670 --> 00:38:44.710
That's what everybody else was doing.

900
00:38:44.710 --> 00:38:47.990
Yeah, and sit at the feet of Neem Karoli Baba,

901
00:38:47.990 --> 00:38:49.870
who essentially, you know,

902
00:38:49.870 --> 00:38:53.510
your platoon leader is a stand in for that type of guru

903
00:38:53.510 --> 00:38:55.720
student teacher, you know, dynamic.

904
00:38:55.720 --> 00:38:56.860
Yeah, yeah.

905
00:38:56.860 --> 00:38:59.345
Yeah, to be honest, I wanted the G.I. Bill,

906
00:38:59.345 --> 00:39:03.050
(both laughing)
and we've not as a Patriot.

907
00:39:03.050 --> 00:39:03.910
Uh-huh.

908
00:39:03.910 --> 00:39:08.280
You know, Vietnam kind of destroyed our military.

909
00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:10.090
Everybody kept saying, "oh, it's such a bad military."

910
00:39:10.090 --> 00:39:11.720
So why don't you join to make it better?

911
00:39:11.720 --> 00:39:13.470
So I was really the kind of guy that said,

912
00:39:13.470 --> 00:39:14.829
hey, we want to rebuild this military,

913
00:39:14.829 --> 00:39:18.160
is gonna be 1% at the time I'm going in and do my part.

914
00:39:18.160 --> 00:39:20.430
So as a Patriot, but more than anything

915
00:39:20.430 --> 00:39:22.640
was a spiritual search and the idea that I landed

916
00:39:22.640 --> 00:39:25.130
from my high school teacher Bishop

917
00:39:25.130 --> 00:39:29.420
into my Marine Corps platoon with Sergeant Throne Berry,

918
00:39:29.420 --> 00:39:32.570
who was, yeah, he was a guru.

919
00:39:32.570 --> 00:39:36.820
It was so unreal to me, Rich.

920
00:39:36.820 --> 00:39:38.880
I mean, truly it was-

921
00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:42.170
You look back, hindsight's always 2020,

922
00:39:42.170 --> 00:39:45.423
and life always makes perfect sense in the rear view mirror,

923
00:39:49.717 --> 00:39:52.396
there's this feeling of predestiny, right?

924
00:39:52.396 --> 00:39:54.070
You're like, you're sort of being prepared

925
00:39:54.070 --> 00:39:56.733
for this life that you live now,

926
00:39:57.750 --> 00:40:01.240
my feeling is that, we all have chance encounters

927
00:40:01.240 --> 00:40:04.270
with great teachers and it's incumbent upon us

928
00:40:04.270 --> 00:40:08.260
to have the awareness to really see and understand

929
00:40:08.260 --> 00:40:09.850
when we're having one of those encounters

930
00:40:09.850 --> 00:40:13.390
so that we can value it and nurture it and appreciate it.

931
00:40:13.390 --> 00:40:14.334
Yeah. I agree with you.

932
00:40:14.334 --> 00:40:19.334
I didn't feel predestination as much as I was working

933
00:40:20.100 --> 00:40:23.363
and doors opened because I was doing the work.

934
00:40:25.490 --> 00:40:28.140
but the doors that opened with Bishop and Throneberry

935
00:40:28.140 --> 00:40:29.933
for example, felt miraculous,

936
00:40:31.070 --> 00:40:33.820
and they defined me as human beings.

937
00:40:33.820 --> 00:40:38.340
So then when it came time for me to go to college,

938
00:40:38.340 --> 00:40:41.010
I wanted to study religion because I wanted to get

939
00:40:41.010 --> 00:40:42.190
at the truth of things.

940
00:40:42.190 --> 00:40:45.413
So I did religion, anthropology, philosophy,

941
00:40:46.550 --> 00:40:48.870
and I had a really good undergraduate degree.

942
00:40:48.870 --> 00:40:50.330
I mean, I was really able to tailor,

943
00:40:50.330 --> 00:40:52.171
make it to my spiritual search.

944
00:40:52.171 --> 00:40:55.067
I read great books and studied with great people.

945
00:40:55.067 --> 00:40:57.556
Was there an idea that you'd be a professor

946
00:40:57.556 --> 00:40:59.352
or what was the sense of career path?

947
00:40:59.352 --> 00:41:02.110
I had no goal other than discover the truth.

948
00:41:02.110 --> 00:41:03.870
I didn't, actually I was a B student in high school.

949
00:41:03.870 --> 00:41:05.900
I didn't know I'd be, so I was this straight A student

950
00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:07.670
in college, I didn't even know I had the aptitude

951
00:41:07.670 --> 00:41:08.503
to tell you the truth.

952
00:41:08.503 --> 00:41:09.561
Yeah.

953
00:41:09.561 --> 00:41:11.240
And then they said professor,

954
00:41:11.240 --> 00:41:13.487
like, "oh, you're professorial."

955
00:41:14.490 --> 00:41:19.490
And I studied religion, and I think I want to be a rabbi.

956
00:41:21.520 --> 00:41:24.170
And my motivation was, I think rabbis sit around

957
00:41:24.170 --> 00:41:25.840
and study ancient tomes.

958
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:26.830
Right.

959
00:41:26.830 --> 00:41:28.620
I forgot they have congregations.

960
00:41:28.620 --> 00:41:30.427
So, when I showed up at Rabbinical School

961
00:41:30.427 --> 00:41:32.410
and I got my slip of paper, here's your congregation,

962
00:41:32.410 --> 00:41:34.121
I said, what?

963
00:41:34.121 --> 00:41:34.954
(both laughing)

964
00:41:34.954 --> 00:41:36.332
You have to get up and talk in front of people.

965
00:41:36.332 --> 00:41:38.000
I gotta go out there and preach.

966
00:41:38.000 --> 00:41:39.980
I thought like, we just kind of steadied

967
00:41:39.980 --> 00:41:42.220
ancient antiquarian books and knew God.

968
00:41:42.220 --> 00:41:44.173
So, I was so naive,

969
00:41:45.342 --> 00:41:48.530
it wasn't until they gave me my assignment

970
00:41:48.530 --> 00:41:51.340
that I remembered, oh, congregational rabbi.

971
00:41:51.340 --> 00:41:52.173
Right.

972
00:41:52.173 --> 00:41:53.006
So.

973
00:41:53.006 --> 00:41:53.839
And that's how it began.

974
00:41:53.839 --> 00:41:54.672
Yeah. That's how it began.

975
00:41:54.672 --> 00:41:55.505
Yeah.

976
00:41:55.505 --> 00:41:57.870
So where, you know, where does the interest

977
00:41:57.870 --> 00:42:02.870
in all these other kinds of strains of thought come in to,

978
00:42:03.430 --> 00:42:05.480
you know, how you practice being a rabbi?

979
00:42:06.600 --> 00:42:09.500
Well, so my religion degree unders...

980
00:42:09.500 --> 00:42:13.080
We focused in the function of religion, not morphology, Jews

981
00:42:13.080 --> 00:42:15.730
and Christianity, Islam, the comparative approach,

982
00:42:15.730 --> 00:42:17.730
but what does religion do?

983
00:42:17.730 --> 00:42:19.053
Organize reality?

984
00:42:20.420 --> 00:42:24.460
So we understood, for example, Marxism is a quasi religion,

985
00:42:24.460 --> 00:42:26.230
which you might call the,

986
00:42:26.230 --> 00:42:27.800
what's happening in politics today.

987
00:42:27.800 --> 00:42:31.090
Some of them are quasi religious because they're in a way

988
00:42:31.090 --> 00:42:33.030
based on things that cannot be empirically shown,

989
00:42:33.030 --> 00:42:34.040
but they believe to exist.

990
00:42:34.040 --> 00:42:36.740
So they have something of a religious quality to them.

991
00:42:37.720 --> 00:42:39.870
So we learned how religion functions.

992
00:42:39.870 --> 00:42:41.720
I also took symbolic anthropology.

993
00:42:41.720 --> 00:42:45.820
So the degree that I cobbled together for myself

994
00:42:45.820 --> 00:42:47.610
was foundational how we understand the world.

995
00:42:47.610 --> 00:42:51.230
Human consciousness, the nature of the symbolic life,

996
00:42:51.230 --> 00:42:52.530
introduction to Carl Jung,

997
00:42:53.850 --> 00:42:57.230
the whole history of philosophical hermeneutics,

998
00:42:57.230 --> 00:42:59.520
how language functions, that connection between language

999
00:42:59.520 --> 00:43:00.643
and consciousness.

1000
00:43:00.643 --> 00:43:03.593
I mean, I really had an extraordinary undergraduate degree.

1001
00:43:06.030 --> 00:43:07.337
Then I went to Rabbinical School for a couple of years,

1002
00:43:07.337 --> 00:43:09.140
and I realized, I don't know enough.

1003
00:43:09.140 --> 00:43:10.830
So I went back and did a doctorate

1004
00:43:10.830 --> 00:43:12.580
in Religion-Social Ethics,

1005
00:43:12.580 --> 00:43:15.010
so I could understand this thing better.

1006
00:43:15.010 --> 00:43:19.050
So, I'm one of those few people I think that my degrees,

1007
00:43:21.550 --> 00:43:25.900
both my undergraduate and PhD were in part of my search

1008
00:43:25.900 --> 00:43:26.763
for truth.

1009
00:43:28.020 --> 00:43:31.040
And I just lucked into the best program

1010
00:43:31.040 --> 00:43:33.000
with the best teachers who at some level,

1011
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.640
let me do what I wanted.

1012
00:43:34.640 --> 00:43:38.960
And so I still am reaping benefits from my undergraduate

1013
00:43:38.960 --> 00:43:41.000
and doctoral program.

1014
00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:44.160
In rabbinical school I mostly learned how to read the text.

1015
00:43:44.160 --> 00:43:46.718
Meaning in rabbinical school, I learned how to do Talmud

1016
00:43:46.718 --> 00:43:49.030
and Midrash and read Aramaic to study the Zohar,

1017
00:43:49.030 --> 00:43:51.830
so that was a very good education

1018
00:43:51.830 --> 00:43:54.853
in accessing the mysteries of the tradition.

1019
00:43:56.260 --> 00:43:58.340
But the intellectual tools

1020
00:43:58.340 --> 00:44:02.147
I got from my two degrees from USC.

1021
00:44:03.660 --> 00:44:08.620
And I would say that trajectory is still moving forward.

1022
00:44:08.620 --> 00:44:09.756
I mean, it is.
Right, right.

1023
00:44:09.756 --> 00:44:12.360
And, and how has your...

1024
00:44:12.360 --> 00:44:14.960
Clearly, the way that you kind of do what you do

1025
00:44:14.960 --> 00:44:18.870
is a little bit askew from the typical rabbi.

1026
00:44:18.870 --> 00:44:22.270
How does the sort of Jewish community perceive you?

1027
00:44:22.270 --> 00:44:24.283
Like, are you considered... Like is it,

1028
00:44:25.530 --> 00:44:28.070
certainly there's different, you know, traditional strains

1029
00:44:28.070 --> 00:44:29.520
and Orthodox and all of that,

1030
00:44:30.360 --> 00:44:33.970
but are you like welcomed as an equal voice

1031
00:44:33.970 --> 00:44:37.583
in this conversation?

1032
00:44:38.870 --> 00:44:42.129
What I hear is I'm highly respected.

1033
00:44:42.129 --> 00:44:43.320
Yeah.
That's what I hear.

1034
00:44:43.320 --> 00:44:45.150
I'm a reform ordained rabbi,

1035
00:44:45.150 --> 00:44:47.180
but I'm not in the social justice thing.

1036
00:44:47.180 --> 00:44:48.840
And there's enough people trying to fix society,

1037
00:44:48.840 --> 00:44:49.960
fix other people I don't need involved in.

1038
