00:56:07.898 --> 00:56:09.910
was not the resilience

1291
00:56:09.910 --> 00:56:11.910
because that kind of came natural to me.

1292
00:56:13.230 --> 00:56:16.160
You know, I mean, there so many Marine Corps legends.

1293
00:56:16.160 --> 00:56:18.710
We hold the line, they will not get any further,

1294
00:56:18.710 --> 00:56:19.690
or I'm gonna die trying.

1295
00:56:19.690 --> 00:56:24.283
That was the mythos into which I was inducted.

1296
00:56:25.960 --> 00:56:27.890
But the idea that there was a rational ordering

1297
00:56:27.890 --> 00:56:32.810
to the universe, and that if you don't align yourself

1298
00:56:32.810 --> 00:56:34.437
with it, you'll suffer unnecessarily,

1299
00:56:34.437 --> 00:56:38.484
that was something that I found really, really profound.

1300
00:56:38.484 --> 00:56:39.317
That is interesting.

1301
00:56:39.317 --> 00:56:41.500
I mean, I've spent quite a bit of time with Ryan Holiday

1302
00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:43.330
and I've read all his books, and I have read

1303
00:56:43.330 --> 00:56:44.750
a fair amount of stoicism,

1304
00:56:44.750 --> 00:56:48.390
but I'm not super familiar with that idea of logos.

1305
00:56:48.390 --> 00:56:50.830
And when you were talking about it,

1306
00:56:50.830 --> 00:56:54.283
I was drawing a comparison between stoicism

1307
00:56:54.283 --> 00:56:59.283
as a philosophy and how that differentiates from religion.

1308
00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:03.150
But on some level, there's a buy-in with respect

1309
00:57:03.150 --> 00:57:04.800
to the logos, right?

1310
00:57:04.800 --> 00:57:07.040
In that you have to believe that there is an order

1311
00:57:07.040 --> 00:57:09.410
of universe and that there are these natural laws

1312
00:57:09.410 --> 00:57:12.790
that are at play that require adherence on your part-

1313
00:57:12.790 --> 00:57:13.623
Precisely.

1314
00:57:13.623 --> 00:57:14.820
Or suffering, right?

1315
00:57:14.820 --> 00:57:18.840
So, on some level, there is a religious flair to that-

1316
00:57:18.840 --> 00:57:21.110
Absolutely, yes.
Philosophical traditions.

1317
00:57:21.110 --> 00:57:22.260
Very well put.

1318
00:57:22.260 --> 00:57:26.300
And that's why there are books on the stoic element

1319
00:57:26.300 --> 00:57:28.810
and rabbinic Judaism, because rabbinic Judaism, for example,

1320
00:57:28.810 --> 00:57:33.810
is mainly propelled by the idea of a mitzvah, a commandment,

1321
00:57:34.120 --> 00:57:35.770
whether you feel like it or not.

1322
00:57:35.770 --> 00:57:36.640
So I'll give you an example.

1323
00:57:36.640 --> 00:57:39.340
There are some Fridays when my wife and I are just exhausted

1324
00:57:39.340 --> 00:57:41.873
from a tough week, but it's Friday.

1325
00:57:43.290 --> 00:57:45.140
So we have to dress up.
Mm-hmm.

1326
00:57:45.140 --> 00:57:47.580
My wife pick flowers, we've gotta set the table.

1327
00:57:47.580 --> 00:57:50.463
We don't feel like it, but Shabbat is a mitzvah.

1328
00:57:51.620 --> 00:57:53.140
So despite what we feel,

1329
00:57:53.140 --> 00:57:55.760
we have to welcome the Sabbath bride into our home,

1330
00:57:55.760 --> 00:57:56.970
which means we set the table,

1331
00:57:56.970 --> 00:57:59.640
we put out the hall of the loaves, we set out the candles,

1332
00:57:59.640 --> 00:58:01.400
my wife picks flowers from the garden,

1333
00:58:01.400 --> 00:58:02.910
and we create a little garden of Eden

1334
00:58:02.910 --> 00:58:04.630
around her dining room table.

1335
00:58:04.630 --> 00:58:06.320
And, you know, our daughters grew up with it,

1336
00:58:06.320 --> 00:58:07.337
it doesn't matter what else is going on.

1337
00:58:07.337 --> 00:58:09.340
You gotta do the deal no matter what.

1338
00:58:09.340 --> 00:58:10.780
You gotta do the deal, exactly.

1339
00:58:10.780 --> 00:58:14.090
The mitzvah is more important than your feelings.

1340
00:58:14.090 --> 00:58:16.410
So this idea, it doesn't matter what I feel.

1341
00:58:16.410 --> 00:58:17.910
Now, look, we're not Orthodox,

1342
00:58:19.340 --> 00:58:21.220
but the idea is, when Friday night comes,

1343
00:58:21.220 --> 00:58:22.810
I don't have a choice.

1344
00:58:22.810 --> 00:58:25.593
I will snap my feelings around my duty.

1345
00:58:26.690 --> 00:58:30.860
So that idea... So, in the idea of mitzvah,

1346
00:58:30.860 --> 00:58:32.763
a wholly urging from God,

1347
00:58:33.660 --> 00:58:36.833
to which in general you can't say no in general,

1348
00:58:38.280 --> 00:58:40.320
is a very stoic idea.

1349
00:58:40.320 --> 00:58:42.420
It's your duty, it has to be done.

1350
00:58:42.420 --> 00:58:43.900
But it's behavior-based.

1351
00:58:43.900 --> 00:58:44.733
Absolutely.
Right.

1352
00:58:44.733 --> 00:58:45.700
And this is where they, you know,

1353
00:58:45.700 --> 00:58:47.670
I'm sure you're familiar the idea of the outside in,

1354
00:58:47.670 --> 00:58:51.120
first you do your duty, and then it sinks in.

1355
00:58:51.120 --> 00:58:51.953
Right.

1356
00:58:51.953 --> 00:58:53.170
'Cause then when you do sit at the table,

1357
00:58:53.170 --> 00:58:55.790
and you sing the songs and you smell the flowers

1358
00:58:55.790 --> 00:58:58.050
and we look at each other and, you know,

1359
00:58:58.050 --> 00:58:59.230
whenever we light the candles,

1360
00:58:59.230 --> 00:59:00.957
I think of the first from Proverbs,

1361
00:59:00.957 --> 00:59:02.640
"The light of God is the human soul."

1362
00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:04.400
And then I look at my wife and kids,

1363
00:59:04.400 --> 00:59:06.920
whoever's at our table and all of a sudden I'm in.

1364
00:59:06.920 --> 00:59:08.420
But you see had I not just said,

1365
00:59:08.420 --> 00:59:12.630
it's a duty that dragged me to the table

1366
00:59:13.860 --> 00:59:15.113
and put the candles out,

1367
00:59:15.950 --> 00:59:19.000
candles are lit, light of God is the human soul,

1368
00:59:19.000 --> 00:59:20.770
consciousness changes.

1369
00:59:20.770 --> 00:59:21.878
You know what I call that?

1370
00:59:21.878 --> 00:59:22.711
What's that?

1371
00:59:22.711 --> 00:59:23.670
Mood follows action.

1372
00:59:23.670 --> 00:59:24.730
Mood follows action, exactly.

1373
00:59:24.730 --> 00:59:26.680
Yeah, which is something I learned in early sobriety.

1374
00:59:26.680 --> 00:59:27.513
There you go.

1375
00:59:27.513 --> 00:59:32.240
So that's for me, a stoic duty snaps you into the logos.

1376
00:59:34.950 --> 00:59:39.950
And now I'm not a Orthodox stoic philosopher.

1377
00:59:41.090 --> 00:59:43.340
So for me, part of the logo says, love, justice,

1378
00:59:43.340 --> 00:59:46.240
truth and beauty and a beauty is a very big part of it.

1379
00:59:46.240 --> 00:59:49.050
So one thing that, you know, for example,

1380
00:59:49.050 --> 00:59:50.490
in the Jewish observance of the Sabbath,

1381
00:59:50.490 --> 00:59:52.060
a big part of it is beauty.

1382
00:59:52.060 --> 00:59:54.220
It's an interesting thing.

1383
00:59:54.220 --> 00:59:56.080
If you don't make your table beautiful,

1384
00:59:56.080 --> 00:59:58.090
you have observed the Sabbath.

1385
00:59:58.090 --> 01:00:00.540
So we have an obligation to create beauty.

1386
01:00:00.540 --> 01:00:01.373
I love that.

1387
01:00:01.373 --> 01:00:02.451
Isn't it?

1388
01:00:02.451 --> 01:00:03.284
Yeah.

1389
01:00:03.284 --> 01:00:04.550
Yeah. So, it's a duty.

1390
01:00:04.550 --> 01:00:07.910
Because beauty is one of the garments of God.

1391
01:00:07.910 --> 01:00:10.610
So how can experience God if you don't cultivate beauty

1392
01:00:10.610 --> 01:00:11.590
in your life?
Mm-hmm.

1393
01:00:11.590 --> 01:00:14.160
That's something I teach a lot, by the way.

1394
01:00:14.160 --> 01:00:16.170
To that person as a spiritual seeker, I said,

1395
01:00:16.170 --> 01:00:18.310
what's your connection with beauty?

1396
01:00:18.310 --> 01:00:19.900
They say, "what does that matter?

1397
01:00:19.900 --> 01:00:21.320
I want truth."

1398
01:00:21.320 --> 01:00:23.790
I say, beauty is a garment of God,

1399
01:00:23.790 --> 01:00:26.783
just as much as love, justice, truth and beauty.

1400
01:00:27.720 --> 01:00:29.400
So you have to cultivate a connection with beauty.

1401
01:00:29.400 --> 01:00:30.730
They say, "what do you recommend?"

1402
01:00:30.730 --> 01:00:32.419
Sergeant peppers (Mordecai laughing)

1403
01:00:32.419 --> 01:00:33.252
Right, right, right.

1404
01:00:33.252 --> 01:00:34.190
Start with what they're already-

1405
01:00:34.190 --> 01:00:35.990
Start with what they know, yeah.

1406
01:00:35.990 --> 01:00:36.878
Right.

1407
01:00:36.878 --> 01:00:41.760
As imperfect beings, we are all as humans,

1408
01:00:41.760 --> 01:00:43.562
a big part of this, I know you've spoken about,

1409
01:00:43.562 --> 01:00:48.270
this is the idea of essentially the daily inventory, right?

1410
01:00:48.270 --> 01:00:51.100
Beginning your day with an objective assessment

1411
01:00:51.100 --> 01:00:55.480
of how you lived your life in the prior 24.

1412
01:00:55.480 --> 01:00:58.440
What does that look like in practice for you?

1413
01:00:58.440 --> 01:00:59.540
So in my practice,

1414
01:00:59.540 --> 01:01:03.410
I actually call this the wisdom practice,

1415
01:01:03.410 --> 01:01:06.920
which is I'm sitting typically on my mat outside

1416
01:01:06.920 --> 01:01:10.340
in the morning, I go to my observer mind,

1417
01:01:10.340 --> 01:01:12.050
I looked down at my ego self,

1418
01:01:12.050 --> 01:01:14.960
and I just run through ego, anger at others,

1419
01:01:14.960 --> 01:01:19.480
anger at myself, resentment, despair, unresolved grief,

1420
01:01:19.480 --> 01:01:23.560
envy, guilt, shame, just, I run across the, you know,

1421
01:01:23.560 --> 01:01:27.210
what I'll call the dirty dozen, you know, whatever they are.

1422
01:01:27.210 --> 01:01:32.210
And when I discover one, it's as if it perks up.

1423
01:01:33.950 --> 01:01:35.963
Says, yeah, I'm active today.

1424
01:01:37.010 --> 01:01:39.300
So then I wanna go in and find out.

1425
01:01:39.300 --> 01:01:41.540
So for example, this is something I teach.

1426
01:01:41.540 --> 01:01:46.540
Anger almost always means a frustrated need, expectation,

1427
01:01:47.170 --> 01:01:48.428
entitlement or demand.

1428
01:01:48.428 --> 01:01:49.261
Right?

1429
01:01:49.261 --> 01:01:51.060
The NEED acronym.
Yeah.

1430
01:01:51.060 --> 01:01:53.540
That's the NEED acronym.

1431
01:01:53.540 --> 01:01:55.380
Everybody who studies with me has to know

1432
01:01:55.380 --> 01:01:56.610
this chapter and verse.

1433
01:01:56.610 --> 01:01:58.023
Okay. So if I'm upset with somebody,

1434
01:01:58.023 --> 01:02:02.863
it's not what they did, is they disappointed my need.

1435
01:02:03.950 --> 01:02:08.150
So I wanna stop being mesmerized by their deeds,

1436
01:02:08.150 --> 01:02:10.053
and focus on my needs.

1437
01:02:11.540 --> 01:02:12.393
All right, now, here's what happens,

1438
01:02:12.393 --> 01:02:14.230
when you focus on your needs,

1439
01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:15.755
your anger goes down 90%.

1440
01:02:15.755 --> 01:02:16.588
Mm-hmm.

1441
01:02:16.588 --> 01:02:18.230
'Cause you're not transfixed by somebody else's behavior.

1442
01:02:18.230 --> 01:02:19.500
So people say, "well, what about what they did?"

1443
01:02:19.500 --> 01:02:21.050
I say, we'll get through them later.

1444
01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:24.390
But is this not all rooted two things?

1445
01:02:24.390 --> 01:02:26.110
First, is this not all rooted

1446
01:02:26.110 --> 01:02:30.360
in expectations around outcomes?

1447
01:02:30.360 --> 01:02:32.598
Sure. Absolutely.
There's that.

1448
01:02:32.598 --> 01:02:36.130
And are not these, all these emotions

1449
01:02:36.130 --> 01:02:37.970
really all rooted in fear?

1450
01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:39.940
Like fear is the antecedent emotion

1451
01:02:39.940 --> 01:02:42.420
from which all of these other sort of-

1452
01:02:42.420 --> 01:02:43.450
Yeah, I'm not convinced of that.

1453
01:02:43.450 --> 01:02:45.157
Sometimes it's domination.
Mm-hmm.

1454
01:02:45.157 --> 01:02:46.610
And sometimes aggressive dominant people

1455
01:02:46.610 --> 01:02:48.150
are not motivated by fear.

1456
01:02:48.150 --> 01:02:50.160
They're just motivated by domination.

1457
01:02:50.160 --> 01:02:51.330
And when they don't get through-

1458
01:02:51.330 --> 01:02:53.610
What does that urge towards domination come from?

1459
01:02:53.610 --> 01:02:55.003
Does it...It's this idea that,

1460
01:02:55.003 --> 01:02:58.830
if somebody else gets that I can't, then.

1461
01:02:58.830 --> 01:03:02.623
You know I think that in the so-called Alpha Being,

1462
01:03:03.690 --> 01:03:05.570
they're not motivated by fear.

1463
01:03:05.570 --> 01:03:08.400
They really ultimately want domination

1464
01:03:08.400 --> 01:03:12.110
and extinguish anybody who stands in their way.

1465
01:03:12.110 --> 01:03:13.210
It's a type of person.

1466
01:03:14.320 --> 01:03:16.760
Now another person says, please stop.

1467
01:03:16.760 --> 01:03:18.140
That's fear.

1468
01:03:18.140 --> 01:03:20.850
The person says, "how dare you disobey me?"

1469
01:03:20.850 --> 01:03:22.100
They're not motivated by fear.

1470
01:03:22.100 --> 01:03:24.990
I think aggression and domination

1471
01:03:24.990 --> 01:03:27.250
are pretty pure as emotions.

1472
01:03:27.250 --> 01:03:29.060
I could be wrong.

1473
01:03:29.060 --> 01:03:29.893
Mm-hmm.

1474
01:03:29.893 --> 01:03:32.330
But I don't think fear is an antecedent emotion.

1475
01:03:32.330 --> 01:03:37.330
I think aggression and dominance over others is primary.

1476
01:03:38.960 --> 01:03:43.320
I could be wrong, but, you know, there are times,

1477
01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:45.083
I suppose I find myself upset.

1478
01:03:46.160 --> 01:03:48.010
You know, like, let's say I've asked my kids to do something

1479
01:03:48.010 --> 01:03:52.520
like super clear, rational, and they just don't do it.

1480
01:03:52.520 --> 01:03:53.540
And I feel angry.

1481
01:03:53.540 --> 01:03:57.810
Like, I asked you to do something clear, rational,

1482
01:03:57.810 --> 01:03:59.633
I was, you know, when,

1483
01:04:00.590 --> 01:04:01.910
and they just decided not to.

1484
01:04:01.910 --> 01:04:03.490
So I see the anger.

1485
01:04:03.490 --> 01:04:04.900
There's no fear there.

1486
01:04:04.900 --> 01:04:06.350
I just don't like being disobeyed.

1487
01:04:06.350 --> 01:04:07.183
Mm-hmm.

1488
01:04:07.183 --> 01:04:08.590
But I don't wanna be an angry guy.

1489
01:04:08.590 --> 01:04:09.423
Okay. So I have a need expectation

1490
01:04:09.423 --> 01:04:14.327
time and demand that my child chose not to perform.

1491
01:04:17.160 --> 01:04:21.480
Now I have to look and so my path is, was my need moral,

1492
01:04:21.480 --> 01:04:23.633
rational, and useful?

1493
01:04:24.990 --> 01:04:27.360
And when it goes to moral, rational, and useful,

1494
01:04:27.360 --> 01:04:29.060
from a rational perspective,

1495
01:04:29.060 --> 01:04:32.470
that's part of the dance with parents and children,

1496
01:04:32.470 --> 01:04:37.470
is children etching out independence by disobedience.

1497
01:04:37.540 --> 01:04:39.200
It's not personal.

1498
01:04:39.200 --> 01:04:42.800
It's part of healthy ego development of a child.

1499
01:04:42.800 --> 01:04:45.460
So if I respond with anger, I'm stunting their growth.

1500
01:04:45.460 --> 01:04:46.660
I'm not helping anybody.

1501
01:04:48.000 --> 01:04:49.200
So I calmed myself down.

1502
01:04:50.220 --> 01:04:51.940
I said, okay, say, can I talk to you a minute?

1503
01:04:51.940 --> 01:04:52.773
Sure.

1504
01:04:52.773 --> 01:04:53.797
I said, so I asked you to do this.

1505
01:04:53.797 --> 01:04:54.650
"Yeah, dad, I'm sorry."

1506
01:04:54.650 --> 01:04:55.483
It's not about sorry now,

1507
01:04:55.483 --> 01:04:57.510
'cause I have my coach hat and I have my authority hat.

1508
01:04:57.510 --> 01:04:59.160
This is the coach hat.

1509
01:04:59.160 --> 01:05:00.809
I want you to look inside yourself

1510
01:05:00.809 --> 01:05:02.580
and I want you to find the meaning of the disobedience.

1511
01:05:02.580 --> 01:05:05.080
See, I found the meaning of my anger,

1512
01:05:05.080 --> 01:05:06.880
but I'm getting rid of it.

1513
01:05:06.880 --> 01:05:08.370
Because what it replaces the anger

1514
01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:10.530
is my calling as a parent,

1515
01:05:10.530 --> 01:05:13.110
which is the parental soul of my child.

1516
01:05:13.110 --> 01:05:14.480
So now I'm calm and I say, okay,

1517
01:05:14.480 --> 01:05:17.570
this is actually a soul moment.

1518
01:05:17.570 --> 01:05:18.810
So my child says, "okay, I'm sorry."

1519
01:05:18.810 --> 01:05:22.886
I said, sorry is for next, right now I want you to ask,

1520
01:05:22.886 --> 01:05:26.710
why that was meaningful to you to disobey me.

1521
01:05:26.710 --> 01:05:28.080
They say, "I don't know."

1522
01:05:28.080 --> 01:05:30.730
I say, I have time.
(Rich laughing)

1523
01:05:30.730 --> 01:05:33.039
I'm just imagining how this would play out with my kids.

1524
01:05:33.039 --> 01:05:34.601
Try it.
They'd be like,

1525
01:05:34.601 --> 01:05:35.461
leave me alone.

1526
01:05:35.461 --> 01:05:36.626
Like I don't know.
No, try now.

1527
01:05:36.626 --> 01:05:37.630
I've been doing it ever since they were seven or eight years

1528
01:05:37.630 --> 01:05:40.370
old and they do something and you say,

1529
01:05:40.370 --> 01:05:43.270
what happened in your inner life

1530
01:05:43.270 --> 01:05:45.270
where that decision made sense?

1531
01:05:45.270 --> 01:05:46.640
Mm-hmm.

1532
01:05:46.640 --> 01:05:47.891
They say, "I don't know."

1533
01:05:47.891 --> 01:05:49.790
I say, I know you don't know.

1534
01:05:49.790 --> 01:05:52.950
And that's what it means to be a child in this family.

1535
01:05:52.950 --> 01:05:53.783
Mm-hmm.

1536
01:05:53.783 --> 01:05:57.890
Because your answer is, let me think or I'll look it up.

1537
01:05:57.890 --> 01:05:58.810
That's something you're all trained.

1538
01:05:58.810 --> 01:05:59.643
Mm-hmm.

1539
01:05:59.643 --> 01:06:02.330
You can say, let me think or I'll look it up,

1540
01:06:02.330 --> 01:06:03.680
after you say I don't know.

1541
01:06:04.722 --> 01:06:09.722
I know that you made this commitment with your kids

1542
01:06:11.700 --> 01:06:13.197
that you were never gonna be angry, right?

1543
01:06:13.197 --> 01:06:15.630
And you put something on one of their doors saying,

1544
01:06:15.630 --> 01:06:17.815
this is like a dad angry free zone or something like that?

1545
01:06:17.815 --> 01:06:19.860
Yeah.
(both laughing)

1546
01:06:19.860 --> 01:06:23.230
Which I loved because it's really, you know,

1547
01:06:23.230 --> 01:06:24.710
it's a challenge to the self, right?

1548
01:06:24.710 --> 01:06:26.000
When you feel that impulse.

1549
01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:30.010
And it made me think about all of these buttons

1550
01:06:30.010 --> 01:06:32.040
that we have installed that are the result

1551
01:06:32.040 --> 01:06:33.740
of the experiences that we've had,

1552
01:06:33.740 --> 01:06:36.100
or the traumas that we've survived,

1553
01:06:36.100 --> 01:06:39.220
wherein when they get pushed, you know,

1554
01:06:39.220 --> 01:06:42.680
logic goes out the window and we just impulsively react.

1555
01:06:42.680 --> 01:06:45.440
And it's only in the aftermath that we can reassess

1556
01:06:45.440 --> 01:06:49.350
or feel guilt or shame, or try to repair whatever damage

1557
01:06:49.350 --> 01:06:52.270
is done, but the trick is like,

1558
01:06:52.270 --> 01:06:55.743
how do you uninstall those buttons or, you know, kind of,

1559
01:06:57.060 --> 01:06:57.980
untrigger them?

1560
01:06:57.980 --> 01:07:00.410
Well, first of all is the virtue practice,

1561
01:07:00.410 --> 01:07:02.193
which is as I call, the Four Cs.

1562
01:07:03.520 --> 01:07:08.010
I started with, I will not anger under any circumstances,

1563
01:07:08.010 --> 01:07:09.293
under any provocation.

1564
01:07:11.600 --> 01:07:14.270
Fine print, I will not criticize people,

1565
01:07:14.270 --> 01:07:16.410
I will not complain to people about their behavior,

1566
01:07:16.410 --> 01:07:17.740
I will not condemn other people,

1567
01:07:17.740 --> 01:07:19.800
I will not engage in escalating conflict.

1568
01:07:19.800 --> 01:07:20.823
Now I fail.

1569
01:07:21.980 --> 01:07:25.020
But if I fail to my standard, I don't have an excuse.

1570
01:07:25.020 --> 01:07:25.863
I just failed.

1571
01:07:27.290 --> 01:07:28.980
Now, I set that every day.

1572
01:07:28.980 --> 01:07:30.580
I mean, when I wake up,

1573
01:07:30.580 --> 01:07:33.760
I will not anger and I will not be defensive.

1574
01:07:33.760 --> 01:07:36.060
I will not criticize, complain, condemn,

1575
01:07:36.060 --> 01:07:38.420
or engage in escalating conflict.

1576
01:07:38.420 --> 01:07:41.630
Someone's upset with me, after a couple of tries,

1577
01:07:41.630 --> 01:07:43.500
I'm not gonna engage what I called the bad JEDDI,

1578
01:07:43.500 --> 01:07:45.423
justifying, explain, I have all these acronyms, okay?

1579
01:07:45.423 --> 01:07:46.970
Bad JEDDI, I've never heard that one.

1580
01:07:46.970 --> 01:07:50.150
Oh yeah, the bad... I will not justify to an angry person

1581
01:07:50.150 --> 01:07:52.440
after I try to explain my point of view

1582
01:07:52.440 --> 01:07:55.050
'cause oftentimes-
I'm sorry, but.

1583
01:07:55.050 --> 01:07:55.980
Never, oh my goodness.

1584
01:07:55.980 --> 01:07:56.813
Someone says that to me,

1585
01:07:56.813 --> 01:07:57.646
all of a sudden I'm like doom squad.

1586
01:07:57.646 --> 01:07:59.000
I will hunt them down.

1587
01:07:59.000 --> 01:08:00.620
I say to people, if you're gonna study with me,

1588
01:08:00.620 --> 01:08:02.880
you never say I'm sorry, but.

1589
01:08:02.880 --> 01:08:04.780
An apology is an apology.

1590
01:08:04.780 --> 01:08:06.260
And by the way, that's a big thing for some people.

1591
01:08:06.260 --> 01:08:09.400
They've actually never heard the gold standard apology.

1592
01:08:09.400 --> 01:08:10.650
Okay?

1593
01:08:10.650 --> 01:08:14.640
So anyway, so, I will not justify explain, defend, deny,

1594
01:08:14.640 --> 01:08:17.050
try to give information to a hostile person.

1595
01:08:17.050 --> 01:08:19.160
So those are my, that's my virtue practice

1596
01:08:19.160 --> 01:08:20.760
under any conditions whatsoever.

1597
01:08:22.560 --> 01:08:27.560
If I find myself upset, I say, okay, I've already committed,

1598
01:08:27.860 --> 01:08:29.450
I'm not gonna do it.

1599
01:08:29.450 --> 01:08:31.253
Now my emotions are not obeying me.

1600
01:08:32.440 --> 01:08:36.380
So what I call the wall of virtue steps between my emotions

1601
01:08:36.380 --> 01:08:38.620
and my speech and behavior, I call this the wall of virtue.

1602
01:08:38.620 --> 01:08:42.560
So I set up a wall of virtue that says, I can have anger,

1603
01:08:42.560 --> 01:08:46.010
I can feel anger, I will not speak it,

1604
01:08:46.010 --> 01:08:47.060
I will not act on it.

1605
01:08:48.150 --> 01:08:48.983
Okay?

1606
01:08:48.983 --> 01:08:50.950
So I say it hits the wall of virtue,

1607
01:08:50.950 --> 01:08:53.210
bounces back into what I call a wisdom mill.

1608
01:08:53.210 --> 01:08:55.264
So I got all kinds of cool names for this stuff.

1609
01:08:55.264 --> 01:08:56.230
Okay?

1610
01:08:56.230 --> 01:08:57.895
So that I set myself up,

1611
01:08:57.895 --> 01:08:59.410
and I have people who I work with, whom I work.

1612
01:08:59.410 --> 01:09:01.640
They tell me about all the escalation and I say, okay,

1613
01:09:01.640 --> 01:09:03.200
wall of virtue time.

1614
01:09:03.200 --> 01:09:05.450
I do this at my... I have a Wednesday night wisdom class.

1615
01:09:05.450 --> 01:09:08.413
And it just began last week, wall of virtue.

1616
01:09:09.520 --> 01:09:11.600
For the regulars, it was a great review.

1617
01:09:11.600 --> 01:09:13.810
For newcomers it was the most stunning thing

1618
01:09:13.810 --> 01:09:15.800
they had ever heard.
(Rich laughing)

1619
01:09:15.800 --> 01:09:16.900
That when you get up in the morning,

1620
01:09:16.900 --> 01:09:19.920
you set up a wall of virtue and there are no exceptions

1621
01:09:19.920 --> 01:09:21.550
and if you fail, you apologize.

1622
01:09:21.550 --> 01:09:22.530
Mm-hmm.

1623
01:09:22.530 --> 01:09:24.271
And that's pretty stoked.

1624
01:09:24.271 --> 01:09:26.230
Yeah, that's a powerful practice.

1625
01:09:26.230 --> 01:09:31.230
I found that meditation and mindfulness go a long way

1626
01:09:31.520 --> 01:09:33.290
towards creating that buffer.

1627
01:09:33.290 --> 01:09:35.300
So, if you visualize it,

1628
01:09:35.300 --> 01:09:39.050
like you're inside of some kind of sphere

1629
01:09:39.050 --> 01:09:41.610
as you navigate the world and like what's gonna bounce off

1630
01:09:41.610 --> 01:09:45.920
and what you're gonna let in, how porous is that membrane,

1631
01:09:45.920 --> 01:09:49.030
mindfulness or a strict meditation practice

1632
01:09:49.030 --> 01:09:54.030
just buys me that little moment of self reflection

1633
01:09:54.130 --> 01:09:55.180
before I act.

1634
01:09:55.180 --> 01:09:58.440
And oftentimes that's the difference between,

1635
01:09:58.440 --> 01:10:00.620
doing something you're gonna regret,

1636
01:10:00.620 --> 01:10:02.980
or aligning your actions with your.

1637
01:10:02.980 --> 01:10:03.813
Exactly.

1638
01:10:03.813 --> 01:10:06.020
So that reflection practice

1639
01:10:06.020 --> 01:10:07.883
is what I call my wisdom practice.

1640
01:10:09.030 --> 01:10:12.820
But the wisdom practice taught me to do the virtue practice

1641
01:10:12.820 --> 01:10:15.570
when I wake up, because what people say is,

1642
01:10:15.570 --> 01:10:16.990
I know I shouldn't have done it,

1643
01:10:16.990 --> 01:10:18.640
my emotions got the better of me.

1644
01:10:19.520 --> 01:10:23.080
I say, so where you reflection creates a wall of virtue,

1645
01:10:23.080 --> 01:10:25.330
and this is actually mind training the brain.

1646
01:10:26.280 --> 01:10:29.180
Because what happens is there's a stimulus and a response.

1647
01:10:30.050 --> 01:10:31.570
So I train people.

1648
01:10:31.570 --> 01:10:33.040
What was the stimulus?

1649
01:10:33.040 --> 01:10:34.430
My child disobeyed me.

1650
01:10:34.430 --> 01:10:35.330
Response, anger.

1651
01:10:35.330 --> 01:10:37.370
I say, no, I want you to try this.

1652
01:10:37.370 --> 01:10:41.230
My child angers me, wall of virtue.

1653
01:10:41.230 --> 01:10:43.713
Train, and its like martial arts.

1654
01:10:44.890 --> 01:10:46.350
You know, like at the beginner in jujitsu,

1655
01:10:46.350 --> 01:10:47.782
someone gets on top of you, what do you want?

1656
01:10:47.782 --> 01:10:48.615
You wanna push them off?

1657
01:10:48.615 --> 01:10:50.160
What does that mean?

1658
01:10:50.160 --> 01:10:50.993
Arm lock.

1659
01:10:52.270 --> 01:10:54.130
The instinct to push somebody off of you

1660
01:10:54.130 --> 01:10:56.710
is inviting an arm lock.

1661
01:10:56.710 --> 01:10:58.660
So whatever you're gonna do in jujitsu,

1662
01:10:58.660 --> 01:11:01.790
do not push someone on top of you 'cause you're saying,

1663
01:11:01.790 --> 01:11:03.123
please arm lock me.

1664
01:11:04.000 --> 01:11:04.870
What would I do instead?

1665
01:11:04.870 --> 01:11:07.660
I say, first you're not gonna do that, right?

1666
01:11:07.660 --> 01:11:08.960
What do you do instead?

1667
01:11:08.960 --> 01:11:11.480
I say, okay, you hide your elbows in your hands

1668
01:11:11.480 --> 01:11:12.630
and you move your hips.

1669
01:11:14.690 --> 01:11:15.700
White belt the next week.

1670
01:11:15.700 --> 01:11:18.000
I keep forgetting because you're a white belt.

1671
01:11:18.840 --> 01:11:19.673
Right.

1672
01:11:19.673 --> 01:11:22.990
So when you feel the instinct to push your arms up,

1673
