01:15:30.523 --> 01:15:31.356
Yeah?

1801
01:15:31.356 --> 01:15:32.189
How often do you train?

1802
01:15:33.750 --> 01:15:34.583
Four times a week.

1803
01:15:34.583 --> 01:15:36.640
Wow, wow.

1804
01:15:36.640 --> 01:15:37.473
Yeah.

1805
01:15:37.473 --> 01:15:39.380
And so what are some of the other lessons

1806
01:15:39.380 --> 01:15:41.330
that you've learned through martial arts

1807
01:15:41.330 --> 01:15:42.863
that find their way into-

1808
01:15:42.863 --> 01:15:47.100
I'd say jujitsu in particular is,

1809
01:15:47.100 --> 01:15:49.293
the way out is not where the pressure is.

1810
01:15:50.810 --> 01:15:52.840
So for example, if someone has mounted me, you know,

1811
01:15:52.840 --> 01:15:55.770
straddled me, and they're pressing down on my neck,

1812
01:15:55.770 --> 01:15:58.990
their hips are light, by definition.

1813
01:15:58.990 --> 01:16:02.530
They can't be equally heavy on their hips and their chest.

1814
01:16:02.530 --> 01:16:05.330
So I feel a chest pressure, I know their hips are light.

1815
01:16:06.750 --> 01:16:07.583
Okay?

1816
01:16:07.583 --> 01:16:10.003
If their hips are heavy, I got space on my chest.

1817
01:16:11.120 --> 01:16:11.953
Okay?

1818
01:16:11.953 --> 01:16:13.420
And so what you learned to do is you kind of feel

1819
01:16:13.420 --> 01:16:16.260
where the other person is, don't get flustered,

1820
01:16:16.260 --> 01:16:17.977
the big thing is, the higher the belt,

1821
01:16:17.977 --> 01:16:19.710
the more calm you stay.

1822
01:16:19.710 --> 01:16:22.150
It doesn't matter what their pressure is.

1823
01:16:22.150 --> 01:16:24.880
And you start to detect where the way out is,

1824
01:16:24.880 --> 01:16:26.580
but you don't respond to pressure.

1825
01:16:27.600 --> 01:16:31.030
When there's pressure you figure out where the escape is.

1826
01:16:31.030 --> 01:16:32.880
So that's one of the main things is,

1827
01:16:32.880 --> 01:16:34.573
stay calm under pressure,

1828
01:16:36.330 --> 01:16:40.380
and slow them down, you know, hooks and angles,

1829
01:16:40.380 --> 01:16:42.740
so you gotta slow their progress down,

1830
01:16:42.740 --> 01:16:43.700
and then from training

1831
01:16:43.700 --> 01:16:45.850
you know where the escape is gonna be.

1832
01:16:45.850 --> 01:16:47.720
So if somebody hasn't made the choke, right, sorry.

1833
01:16:47.720 --> 01:16:48.615
Right.

1834
01:16:48.615 --> 01:16:50.120
If somebody has made a choke,

1835
01:16:50.120 --> 01:16:53.200
I can tell by their choke what my escape is gonna be.

1836
01:16:53.200 --> 01:16:55.220
So first of all I don't get flustered,

1837
01:16:55.220 --> 01:16:57.610
I just know that if someone's choking you,

1838
01:16:57.610 --> 01:17:00.380
they're both putting a move on and they're also giving

1839
01:17:00.380 --> 01:17:02.050
something up, by definition.

1840
01:17:02.050 --> 01:17:03.640
And extrapolating on that,

1841
01:17:03.640 --> 01:17:06.084
where's the wisdom that's applicable in other areas of life?

1842
01:17:06.084 --> 01:17:09.520
Okay, so, for example, the spouse is pressing on you.

1843
01:17:09.520 --> 01:17:10.353
So I get this.

1844
01:17:10.353 --> 01:17:12.990
Where the spouse is angry and pressing on you,

1845
01:17:12.990 --> 01:17:16.143
they wanna throw their arms out, stop, stop!

1846
01:17:17.140 --> 01:17:20.070
And so the idea is distract.

1847
01:17:20.070 --> 01:17:21.513
Say, could you repeat that?

1848
01:17:23.360 --> 01:17:24.193
What?

1849
01:17:24.193 --> 01:17:26.803
No. That what you just said, that was really important.

1850
01:17:26.803 --> 01:17:27.636
I don't know what I just said.

1851
01:17:27.636 --> 01:17:29.510
We'll try to remember, honey.

1852
01:17:29.510 --> 01:17:32.070
And all of a sudden their ego self is just spinning

1853
01:17:32.070 --> 01:17:33.850
because someone just said, can you repeat it?

1854
01:17:33.850 --> 01:17:34.683
So when you ask one to repeat something,

1855
01:17:34.683 --> 01:17:37.460
they got their eyes go up into the archive,

1856
01:17:37.460 --> 01:17:40.790
and their anger plummets 90%, it's a move.

1857
01:17:40.790 --> 01:17:42.940
So there are many scripts for deescalation.

1858
01:17:43.820 --> 01:17:46.033
So fear does not help.

1859
01:17:47.030 --> 01:17:48.780
So I say to people, are they gonna hit you?

1860
01:17:48.780 --> 01:17:49.613
No.

1861
01:17:50.545 --> 01:17:51.378
If they're gonna hit you,

1862
01:17:51.378 --> 01:17:52.540
we're having a different conversation.

1863
01:17:52.540 --> 01:17:55.180
Right. Okay, so your body's gone into fear

1864
01:17:55.180 --> 01:17:56.719
because of their aggression, yes.

1865
01:17:56.719 --> 01:17:58.130
And you know you're not gonna hit, right?

1866
01:17:58.130 --> 01:17:59.140
Get it, yes.

1867
01:17:59.140 --> 01:18:01.260
Okay, I'm gonna teach you some scripts

1868
01:18:01.260 --> 01:18:03.323
that are similar to jujitsu moves.

1869
01:18:05.190 --> 01:18:06.810
And so there are scripts you can use

1870
01:18:06.810 --> 01:18:10.093
with a brain of an angry person that almost invaluable.

1871
01:18:11.080 --> 01:18:14.060
That lead to deescalation through distraction.

1872
01:18:14.060 --> 01:18:16.460
Yeah, in boxing we call it deflection.

1873
01:18:16.460 --> 01:18:17.540
Like I don't wanna hit somebody,

1874
01:18:17.540 --> 01:18:19.890
but I know how to bob and weave and deflect.

1875
01:18:19.890 --> 01:18:21.190
So when people say, well, they said this,

1876
01:18:21.190 --> 01:18:23.040
I say, and so I said this, I saw you hit him back.

1877
01:18:23.040 --> 01:18:24.350
I said, don't do that.

1878
01:18:24.350 --> 01:18:25.183
Yeah.

1879
01:18:25.183 --> 01:18:26.016
Just deflect.

1880
01:18:26.016 --> 01:18:29.680
Bob, weave, through deescalation techniques.

1881
01:18:29.680 --> 01:18:31.680
So sometimes I actually train a person

1882
01:18:31.680 --> 01:18:33.833
in five deescalation techniques.

1883
01:18:34.820 --> 01:18:37.430
So the thing is, I'm being threatened,

1884
01:18:37.430 --> 01:18:39.110
I have to be defensive.

1885
01:18:39.110 --> 01:18:40.660
I get scared.

1886
01:18:40.660 --> 01:18:42.630
All right. First thing is jujitsu, calm down.

1887
01:18:42.630 --> 01:18:43.463
Mm-hmm.

1888
01:18:43.463 --> 01:18:44.296
Just calm down.

1889
01:18:44.296 --> 01:18:45.400
Where you gotta go back to the wall of virtue.

1890
01:18:45.400 --> 01:18:46.664
There you go.
Right.

1891
01:18:46.664 --> 01:18:47.497
That's it.

1892
01:18:47.497 --> 01:18:48.710
If you don't have that then you're just gonna, you know,

1893
01:18:48.710 --> 01:18:50.330
succumb to your base-
Exactly.

1894
01:18:50.330 --> 01:18:52.232
So one wall of virtue is for the angry person

1895
01:18:52.232 --> 01:18:54.640
and the other one is for the defensive person is,

1896
01:18:54.640 --> 01:18:57.230
you feel fear, go to your wall of virtue.

1897
01:18:57.230 --> 01:18:58.653
I'm physically safe.

1898
01:18:59.670 --> 01:19:02.300
Don't let this thing escalate.

1899
01:19:02.300 --> 01:19:04.383
Therefore, if you feel fear from a person

1900
01:19:04.383 --> 01:19:07.510
who's not gonna hurt you, your job is to deescalate

1901
01:19:07.510 --> 01:19:08.630
not to defend yourself.

1902
01:19:08.630 --> 01:19:10.030
They're two different things.

1903
01:19:10.030 --> 01:19:12.520
So the white belt wants to defend,

1904
01:19:12.520 --> 01:19:15.010
the higher belt wants to deescalate.

1905
01:19:15.010 --> 01:19:16.784
And it's a learnable skill.

1906
01:19:16.784 --> 01:19:18.056
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

1907
01:19:18.056 --> 01:19:19.830
So there was an example where,

1908
01:19:19.830 --> 01:19:21.970
what your white belt self wants to do

1909
01:19:21.970 --> 01:19:23.480
is not what the higher belt self knows

1910
01:19:23.480 --> 01:19:24.510
is the right thing to do.

1911
01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:25.343
And how do you do it?

1912
01:19:25.343 --> 01:19:27.860
Train, train, train, train.

1913
01:19:27.860 --> 01:19:31.740
Are you the only rabbi that has a black belt in jujitsu?

1914
01:19:31.740 --> 01:19:32.573
So far.

1915
01:19:32.573 --> 01:19:35.370
Yeah.
(both laughing)

1916
01:19:35.370 --> 01:19:37.030
No one else has come forth yet?

1917
01:19:37.030 --> 01:19:38.440
And once they get it, they're coming for me.

1918
01:19:38.440 --> 01:19:39.273
I know that-

1919
01:19:39.273 --> 01:19:40.510
All you rabbis listening out there,

1920
01:19:40.510 --> 01:19:41.418
the challenge has been placed.

1921
01:19:41.418 --> 01:19:43.770
You know, when I got my black belt, man,

1922
01:19:43.770 --> 01:19:45.610
I was a hunted person.

1923
01:19:45.610 --> 01:19:46.896
Yeah.
(Rabbi laughing)

1924
01:19:46.896 --> 01:19:47.800
That's the nature of the game.

1925
01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:49.320
Everybody wants to snag the first black belt, so.

1926
01:19:49.320 --> 01:19:50.282
Right.

1927
01:19:50.282 --> 01:19:52.450
It's a really cool thing.

1928
01:19:52.450 --> 01:19:53.283
I love it, man.

1929
01:19:53.283 --> 01:19:54.600
I really, you know, I go in there and...

1930
01:19:54.600 --> 01:19:55.910
Like guys are very respectful.

1931
01:19:55.910 --> 01:19:58.607
Like they know I'm 66 and, you know,

1932
01:19:58.607 --> 01:20:00.930
I have bad shoulders and a bad back and-

1933
01:20:00.930 --> 01:20:03.340
But you're grappling with younger dudes.

1934
01:20:03.340 --> 01:20:05.590
I would imagine-
Big young guys and,

1935
01:20:05.590 --> 01:20:07.650
they're respectful but, they're there to train.

1936
01:20:07.650 --> 01:20:09.260
So I can't say, Hey, be nice to the old guy.

1937
01:20:09.260 --> 01:20:10.677
I just say, just be careful with the old.

1938
01:20:10.677 --> 01:20:11.630
Right, right.

1939
01:20:11.630 --> 01:20:13.720
But they're there to train and I gotta respect that.

1940
01:20:13.720 --> 01:20:15.770
So, I need to be a good training partner.

1941
01:20:15.770 --> 01:20:18.083
I needed, you know, we're sparring.

1942
01:20:18.083 --> 01:20:19.040
Right.

1943
01:20:19.040 --> 01:20:20.350
Right, right, right.

1944
01:20:20.350 --> 01:20:24.490
For people that come in for your counseling,

1945
01:20:24.490 --> 01:20:28.410
I would imagine a lot of couples or people that are divorced

1946
01:20:28.410 --> 01:20:30.950
or on the precipice of getting divorced.

1947
01:20:30.950 --> 01:20:33.923
What are the kinds of things that you're commonly seeing?

1948
01:20:35.300 --> 01:20:36.653
Escalating arguments.

1949
01:20:38.330 --> 01:20:39.760
Sometimes taught in therapy to talk

1950
01:20:39.760 --> 01:20:40.593
about their feelings,

1951
01:20:40.593 --> 01:20:42.493
which is one of the worst things you can do

1952
01:20:42.493 --> 01:20:47.453
when, you know, things are rocky.

1953
01:20:49.170 --> 01:20:51.590
So they say, "well, I told my spouse how I felt."

1954
01:20:51.590 --> 01:20:52.690
I said, don't do that.

1955
01:20:53.630 --> 01:20:56.007
In the beginning don't talk about your feelings.

1956
01:20:56.007 --> 01:20:56.960
"So what do I talk about?"

1957
01:20:56.960 --> 01:20:59.950
I say, what exactly do you want them to do or not do

1958
01:20:59.950 --> 01:21:03.423
in one sentence with a clean motivation and a clear goal?

1959
01:21:04.577 --> 01:21:06.890
"Well, I don't want them to get," so I said,

1960
01:21:06.890 --> 01:21:11.830
what exactly do you want them to do now

1961
01:21:11.830 --> 01:21:15.163
with a clean motivation and a clear goal that is observable?

1962
01:21:16.550 --> 01:21:19.830
And people are just so perplexed.

1963
01:21:19.830 --> 01:21:24.731
The idea of, it's not about my feelings

1964
01:21:24.731 --> 01:21:25.564
what would you like them to do?

1965
01:21:25.564 --> 01:21:27.520
So one person says, "well, I would like my husband

1966
01:21:27.520 --> 01:21:28.353
to apologize."

1967
01:21:28.353 --> 01:21:29.186
I said, go ask them.

1968
01:21:29.186 --> 01:21:33.020
Say, honey, I'd like to apologize for what you said.

1969
01:21:33.020 --> 01:21:34.480
And look at him.

1970
01:21:34.480 --> 01:21:35.313
He said, "I don't have to apologize."

1971
01:21:35.313 --> 01:21:36.527
You just say no.

1972
01:21:37.645 --> 01:21:39.530
Say no. You don't have to go into a big story.

1973
01:21:39.530 --> 01:21:42.560
Just say, I choose to not apologize.

1974
01:21:42.560 --> 01:21:44.950
I look at, let's say the woman in this case of this couple,

1975
01:21:44.950 --> 01:21:46.813
I'll say, now you'll have to learn to take no for an answer.

1976
01:21:46.813 --> 01:21:47.803
It's a skill.

1977
01:21:48.840 --> 01:21:51.140
Take no for an answer.

1978
01:21:51.140 --> 01:21:55.040
I'd like you to apologize, I choose not to, okay.

1979
01:21:55.040 --> 01:21:56.810
But how can I take no for an answer?

1980
01:21:56.810 --> 01:21:58.890
Because anything you say next will escalate

1981
01:21:58.890 --> 01:22:00.610
and you'll be back where you started.

1982
01:22:00.610 --> 01:22:02.770
But is there not room for acknowledging

1983
01:22:02.770 --> 01:22:06.491
the feelings in the context of making that ask?

1984
01:22:06.491 --> 01:22:07.668
'Cause if you were to say,

1985
01:22:07.668 --> 01:22:11.000
listen, the reason I'm asking for this apology

1986
01:22:11.000 --> 01:22:14.730
is because when you did this, it made me feel unseen

1987
01:22:14.730 --> 01:22:19.250
or like if you could like get past the reactionary response

1988
01:22:19.250 --> 01:22:21.480
in the moment to what's behind it,

1989
01:22:21.480 --> 01:22:24.230
like I feel unappreciated or whatever the case may be-

1990
01:22:24.230 --> 01:22:26.134
After about a month, after about a month.

1991
01:22:26.134 --> 01:22:29.490
Because what will happen if you say, I feel unseen?

1992
01:22:29.490 --> 01:22:30.323
Oh, right.

1993
01:22:30.323 --> 01:22:31.790
I'm not appreciated, you're not appreciated.

1994
01:22:31.790 --> 01:22:32.650
I'm not appreciated.

1995
01:22:32.650 --> 01:22:34.603
So what you start with is minimal.

1996
01:22:35.470 --> 01:22:36.790
I'd like you to apologize.

1997
01:22:36.790 --> 01:22:37.720
I choose not to.

1998
01:22:37.720 --> 01:22:39.570
I can take no for an answer.

1999
01:22:39.570 --> 01:22:41.890
Wow, no one got their eyebrows cinched

2000
01:22:42.820 --> 01:22:45.380
and is incremental like jujitsu.

2001
01:22:45.380 --> 01:22:46.930
White belt, white belt, white belt,

2002
01:22:46.930 --> 01:22:48.640
put a Stripe on your white belt.

2003
01:22:48.640 --> 01:22:49.582
More moves, more move, more, put another S

2004
01:22:49.582 --> 01:22:50.570
tripe.

2005
01:22:50.570 --> 01:22:51.915
And eventually when your blue belt,

2006
01:22:51.915 --> 01:22:52.790
you can talk about your feelings.

2007
01:22:52.790 --> 01:22:53.860
Mm-hmm.

2008
01:22:53.860 --> 01:22:55.103
So what I've discovered is,

2009
01:22:55.103 --> 01:22:58.850
many people think they have higher belt skills,

2010
01:22:58.850 --> 01:23:00.510
but the minute they try to use those,

2011
01:23:00.510 --> 01:23:03.070
here's how I feel, I don't feel seen and appreciated,

2012
01:23:03.070 --> 01:23:04.233
things escalate.

2013
01:23:05.400 --> 01:23:07.334
So my job is deescalation.

2014
01:23:07.334 --> 01:23:10.010
I say, you will talk about your feelings

2015
01:23:10.010 --> 01:23:13.300
when you both know how to talk about your feelings,

2016
01:23:13.300 --> 01:23:14.750
and you both know how to listen to the feelings

2017
01:23:14.750 --> 01:23:17.830
of another person without getting defensive

2018
01:23:17.830 --> 01:23:20.380
and then wanting to pile on, which is very typical.

2019
01:23:21.330 --> 01:23:23.380
So, you've intuited something correct.

2020
01:23:23.380 --> 01:23:24.920
Many people don't like this.

2021
01:23:24.920 --> 01:23:26.540
They say, "I have to talk about my feelings."

2022
01:23:26.540 --> 01:23:27.740
I say, can you wait a month?

2023
01:23:27.740 --> 01:23:28.890
They say, "no, I can't wait a month."

2024
01:23:28.890 --> 01:23:30.520
I say, okay, so, I'm not the guy.

2025
01:23:30.520 --> 01:23:31.530
Hmm.

2026
01:23:31.530 --> 01:23:33.340
Because this is stoicism.

2027
01:23:33.340 --> 01:23:34.173
Mm-hmm.

2028
01:23:34.173 --> 01:23:35.164
Right?

2029
01:23:35.164 --> 01:23:37.040
What's the natural order of things?

2030
01:23:37.040 --> 01:23:39.280
When things are spiraling apart,

2031
01:23:39.280 --> 01:23:42.180
you don't get to say whatever you want.

2032
01:23:42.180 --> 01:23:45.053
You gotta be careful until you build up trust,

2033
01:23:45.930 --> 01:23:49.230
you build up a good rhythm for good communication,

2034
01:23:49.230 --> 01:23:51.800
and then learn how to introduce those things slowly.

2035
01:23:51.800 --> 01:23:52.633
Hmm.

2036
01:23:52.633 --> 01:23:55.030
So I'm a big believer in,

2037
01:23:55.030 --> 01:23:58.570
when things are careening out of control,

2038
01:23:58.570 --> 01:24:00.140
everybody talking minimum.

2039
01:24:00.140 --> 01:24:00.973
Hmm.

2040
01:24:02.010 --> 01:24:06.383
So what do you say to the person who comes to you and says,

2041
01:24:07.277 --> 01:24:11.610
"you wouldn't believe what my ex-husband, ex-wife did.

2042
01:24:11.610 --> 01:24:14.230
They're doing this, they're doing that and it's terrible,

2043
01:24:14.230 --> 01:24:15.970
and I don't get to see my kids,

2044
01:24:15.970 --> 01:24:18.880
and, you know, they're telling all these other people

2045
01:24:18.880 --> 01:24:21.340
all these lies," there's a whole story, right?

2046
01:24:21.340 --> 01:24:23.490
And there's an attachment to that story.

2047
01:24:23.490 --> 01:24:28.490
And there's a perverted kind of,

2048
01:24:30.490 --> 01:24:32.203
what's the word I'm looking for?

2049
01:24:35.670 --> 01:24:39.850
Kind of attachment to how that story is received

2050
01:24:39.850 --> 01:24:41.190
when told to friends, right?

2051
01:24:41.190 --> 01:24:42.680
There's an out...And you get affirmed like,

2052
01:24:42.680 --> 01:24:47.040
oh, it's so bad, and you're right and that person's wrong.

2053
01:24:47.040 --> 01:24:51.270
Like teasing that apart and trying to get to an objective

2054
01:24:51.270 --> 01:24:52.460
truth with that person-

2055
01:24:52.460 --> 01:24:53.670
Sure, so first thing I say,

2056
01:24:53.670 --> 01:24:55.220
well, how's that going for you?

2057
01:24:57.000 --> 01:24:58.852
Meaning having the story in your head and acting on it,

2058
01:24:58.852 --> 01:25:01.543
