2312
01:34:26.012 --> 01:34:30.320
can you recreate something that happened with a parent,

2313
01:34:30.320 --> 01:34:34.370
a spouse, a child that made you wanna relapse?

2314
01:34:34.370 --> 01:34:37.463
And can we process it through wisdom?

2315
01:34:38.388 --> 01:34:39.600
And so that's a typical session.

2316
01:34:39.600 --> 01:34:40.904
Is I'll present an idea and someone says,

2317
01:34:40.904 --> 01:34:42.386
"yeah, I want to process this.

2318
01:34:42.386 --> 01:34:45.570
And, you know, this made me so angry

2319
01:34:45.570 --> 01:34:46.690
and this made me depressed."

2320
01:34:46.690 --> 01:34:49.220
I said, okay, so let's process it with higher self

2321
01:34:49.220 --> 01:34:52.920
observing ego self, and doing an intervention,

2322
01:34:52.920 --> 01:34:55.100
coming out with something wise.

2323
01:34:55.100 --> 01:35:00.100
So, I mean, that's a barebone sketch of what I do

2324
01:35:00.417 --> 01:35:03.140
and what actually comes out in the room is sometimes quite-

2325
01:35:03.140 --> 01:35:06.150
But I would suspect there's a great receptivity though,

2326
01:35:06.150 --> 01:35:08.700
because anybody who's worked the steps specifically,

2327
01:35:08.700 --> 01:35:11.330
the Four step knows how to perform an inventory

2328
01:35:11.330 --> 01:35:15.650
and has engaged that muscle of trying to parse, you know,

2329
01:35:15.650 --> 01:35:18.650
what's my part in every situation that occurs?

2330
01:35:18.650 --> 01:35:21.410
Where can I find, you know, how I contributed to this,

2331
01:35:21.410 --> 01:35:23.484
you know, terrible outcome?

2332
01:35:23.484 --> 01:35:26.780
Where am I displaying fear, anger, resentment,

2333
01:35:26.780 --> 01:35:28.240
like it would lead to all of these sorts of things.

2334
01:35:28.240 --> 01:35:30.830
Yeah, so 12 steps really helps them in that.

2335
01:35:30.830 --> 01:35:34.523
So in many ways, there are already being propelled,

2336
01:35:36.560 --> 01:35:37.570
but I'll give you an example.

2337
01:35:37.570 --> 01:35:42.273
So, a guy borrowed the parent's car and it ran out of gas.

2338
01:35:43.710 --> 01:35:47.240
And so of course the parents, you're irresponsible,

2339
01:35:47.240 --> 01:35:49.040
all this insults and he flipped out.

2340
01:35:50.690 --> 01:35:52.823
I said, okay, let's just go deep inside.

2341
01:35:54.380 --> 01:35:56.773
What did you want your parents to do or not do?

2342
01:35:57.777 --> 01:35:59.010
"I didn't want them to criticize me.

2343
01:35:59.010 --> 01:36:00.780
I was in enough trouble already with a car out of gas."

2344
01:36:00.780 --> 01:36:01.693
I say, got it.

2345
01:36:02.537 --> 01:36:04.260
What's the likelihood that they are at this point

2346
01:36:04.260 --> 01:36:07.890
in their lives, they would know how not to blame

2347
01:36:07.890 --> 01:36:10.120
and accuse you when you did something they didn't like?

2348
01:36:10.120 --> 01:36:12.140
Where are they at in their moral development?

2349
01:36:12.140 --> 01:36:15.090
He said, "it would be impossible for them."

2350
01:36:15.090 --> 01:36:17.660
So your need, expectation and entitlement

2351
01:36:17.660 --> 01:36:18.810
was not connected to reality?

2352
01:36:18.810 --> 01:36:19.643
Mm-hmm.

2353
01:36:19.643 --> 01:36:20.762
Okay?

2354
01:36:20.762 --> 01:36:21.595
He says, "what do I do?"

2355
01:36:21.595 --> 01:36:23.570
I say, you feel incredibly sad.

2356
01:36:23.570 --> 01:36:24.592
Well, what do I say?

2357
01:36:24.592 --> 01:36:25.425
He said, "yeah, you're right.

2358
01:36:25.425 --> 01:36:26.258
I should have been more thoughtful."

2359
01:36:26.258 --> 01:36:27.091
Well, you're not responsible.

2360
01:36:27.091 --> 01:36:28.220
"I know I'm not responsible."

2361
01:36:28.220 --> 01:36:29.053
Well, what are you doing about it?

2362
01:36:29.053 --> 01:36:30.690
"I'm in recovery program."

2363
01:36:30.690 --> 01:36:32.427
Well, don't you think you should be responsible by now?

2364
01:36:32.427 --> 01:36:34.140
"Yeah, I should be but I'm working on it."

2365
01:36:34.140 --> 01:36:36.510
Just deflect, deflect, deflect, deflect, deflect.

2366
01:36:36.510 --> 01:36:37.710
They're gonna calm down.

2367
01:36:39.176 --> 01:36:40.009
And he said, "well."

2368
01:36:40.009 --> 01:36:41.650
And then afterwards you can say, hey, mom, dad,

2369
01:36:41.650 --> 01:36:42.483
can I have a minute of your time?

2370
01:36:42.483 --> 01:36:43.661
Sure.

2371
01:36:43.661 --> 01:36:44.494
"I want you to know I really felt horrible

2372
01:36:44.494 --> 01:36:46.560
when I ran out of gas, I know it's my old self

2373
01:36:46.560 --> 01:36:47.760
that doesn't plan ahead,

2374
01:36:48.610 --> 01:36:51.683
but I want you to tell me that when you guys piled on me,

2375
01:36:54.247 --> 01:36:57.147
it didn't feel good, and it didn't make it better for me."

2376
01:36:58.303 --> 01:36:59.136
"Well, what do you expect us to do?"

2377
01:36:59.136 --> 01:36:59.969
Right.

2378
01:36:59.969 --> 01:37:01.485
That's all I needed to say.

2379
01:37:01.485 --> 01:37:03.590
And then they come down to the center and we say,

2380
01:37:03.590 --> 01:37:04.690
don't do that anymore.

2381
01:37:05.640 --> 01:37:08.630
When your kid gets in trouble, you got a kid in trouble,

2382
01:37:08.630 --> 01:37:11.625
this is not the day that the parents pile on,

2383
01:37:11.625 --> 01:37:12.458
it's the day where the parents say,

2384
01:37:12.458 --> 01:37:13.810
"well, you probably feel bad enough already.

2385
01:37:13.810 --> 01:37:14.981
What can we do?"

2386
01:37:14.981 --> 01:37:15.814
Sure.

2387
01:37:15.814 --> 01:37:16.800
So this is a whole retraining of the parent brain.

2388
01:37:16.800 --> 01:37:17.960
Sure.

2389
01:37:17.960 --> 01:37:21.970
But the JEDDI, from the perspective of the kid in recovery,

2390
01:37:21.970 --> 01:37:24.840
the JEDDI move is to not be ruffled

2391
01:37:24.840 --> 01:37:26.780
by whatever the parents say.

2392
01:37:26.780 --> 01:37:31.780
And I think there's value in mining that need even deeper.

2393
01:37:32.720 --> 01:37:34.440
It's not just, hey, you know,

2394
01:37:34.440 --> 01:37:35.830
I didn't want my parents to get mad at me.

2395
01:37:35.830 --> 01:37:39.540
Like there's a deeper need, which is likely, you know,

2396
01:37:39.540 --> 01:37:40.807
I've been a fuck up for a long time

2397
01:37:40.807 --> 01:37:42.200
and I screwed up a lot of stuff

2398
01:37:42.200 --> 01:37:45.480
and now I'm sober and I wanna be perceived as such.

2399
01:37:45.480 --> 01:37:46.910
And I can't get a break.

2400
01:37:46.910 --> 01:37:48.280
Like, no matter what I do,

2401
01:37:48.280 --> 01:37:49.113
it's never gonna be good enough

2402
01:37:49.113 --> 01:37:51.230
or they're never gonna see me, you know.

2403
01:37:51.230 --> 01:37:54.041
Yeah, you're 100% right on it, 100% right on it.

2404
01:37:54.041 --> 01:37:55.440
And that's where the conversation goes.

2405
01:37:55.440 --> 01:37:56.640
When are they gonna give me a break?

2406
01:37:56.640 --> 01:37:59.660
And I say, we're gonna have to work

2407
01:37:59.660 --> 01:38:02.543
with you and your JEDDI skill,

2408
01:38:03.620 --> 01:38:06.140
and then we're gonna work with the parents,

2409
01:38:06.140 --> 01:38:07.690
and you're gonna be able

2410
01:38:07.690 --> 01:38:09.160
to just sometimes say your little truth to the parents

2411
01:38:09.160 --> 01:38:14.160
and say, I really am in a program and I'm really working it.

2412
01:38:14.320 --> 01:38:16.320
And that I would love it if you guys would give me

2413
01:38:16.320 --> 01:38:18.200
a good word or a little bit of patient with me,

2414
01:38:18.200 --> 01:38:20.660
'cause what you want out of me is what I want out of me.

2415
01:38:20.660 --> 01:38:24.500
And sometimes the parent says, "wow, you're right.

2416
01:38:24.500 --> 01:38:26.640
You are doing what we want you to do

2417
01:38:26.640 --> 01:38:28.900
and we're not making it easy on you."

2418
01:38:28.900 --> 01:38:31.280
And, I mean, these are moments that are almost miraculous

2419
01:38:31.280 --> 01:38:32.877
when the kid comes back to me and says,

2420
01:38:32.877 --> 01:38:34.661
"you would not believe the conversation

2421
01:38:34.661 --> 01:38:36.560
I had with my father."

2422
01:38:36.560 --> 01:38:37.393
Right.

2423
01:38:37.393 --> 01:38:38.227
I was able to stay calm and say,

2424
01:38:38.227 --> 01:38:39.773
"Hey, dad, you're 100% right,

2425
01:38:41.000 --> 01:38:42.467
but I'm working the program."

2426
01:38:42.467 --> 01:38:44.740
And for the dad to say, "I really apologize."

2427
01:38:44.740 --> 01:38:45.620
It wasn't helpful, was it?

2428
01:38:45.620 --> 01:38:46.453
Yeah.

2429
01:38:46.453 --> 01:38:49.290
And the kid says, "wow, it's just like a new dawn."

2430
01:38:49.290 --> 01:38:51.440
Yeah. It seems like such a small thing,

2431
01:38:51.440 --> 01:38:52.610
but that's a really big deal.

2432
01:38:52.610 --> 01:38:57.610
Yeah. So managing that moment of anger and defensiveness,

2433
01:38:57.880 --> 01:39:01.900
centering yourself, the deescalating,

2434
01:39:01.900 --> 01:39:03.950
you're right, dad, you're right, mom,

2435
01:39:03.950 --> 01:39:06.020
that was irresponsible of me.

2436
01:39:06.020 --> 01:39:06.853
You're right.

2437
01:39:06.853 --> 01:39:07.686
Well, what are you doing about it?

2438
01:39:07.686 --> 01:39:09.120
"I'm in recovery."

2439
01:39:09.120 --> 01:39:10.547
Well, when are you gonna stop doing this?

2440
01:39:10.547 --> 01:39:12.150
"I hope soon."

2441
01:39:12.150 --> 01:39:13.373
Well, why aren't you doing it now?

2442
01:39:13.373 --> 01:39:14.997
(Rich laughing)
"'Cause I'm not there yet."

2443
01:39:16.500 --> 01:39:18.880
They go, "okay, all right."
(Rich laughing)

2444
01:39:18.880 --> 01:39:19.713
Yeah.

2445
01:39:19.713 --> 01:39:20.546
Right.

2446
01:39:20.546 --> 01:39:22.070
So you understand that when,

2447
01:39:22.070 --> 01:39:24.720
it's all the guys, when they learn this stuff,

2448
01:39:24.720 --> 01:39:28.620
it's like, wow, I can just be calm, JEDDI,

2449
01:39:28.620 --> 01:39:32.560
deflect, deflect, deescalate, and you come out of it.

2450
01:39:32.560 --> 01:39:34.140
Mm-hmm.

2451
01:39:34.140 --> 01:39:35.650
And then you start to go in with wisdom.

2452
01:39:35.650 --> 01:39:39.533
So it's really, I mean, the guys for whom this works,

2453
01:39:40.400 --> 01:39:44.206
they are so grateful and transformed by the things

2454
01:39:44.206 --> 01:39:46.530
that you and I were talking about here today.

2455
01:39:46.530 --> 01:39:47.799
It's hard though.

2456
01:39:47.799 --> 01:39:49.140
It takes a lot of work.

2457
01:39:49.140 --> 01:39:53.129
I mean, especially when you're newly sober and you no longer

2458
01:39:53.129 --> 01:39:55.227
can hide with your best friend,

2459
01:39:55.227 --> 01:39:56.730
and you don't have that coping mechanism.

2460
01:39:56.730 --> 01:39:59.250
You're just this live wire,

2461
01:39:59.250 --> 01:40:02.390
ready to pounce at anything and everything's on the surface.

2462
01:40:02.390 --> 01:40:06.473
And that's place where I teach recover integrity.

2463
01:40:07.600 --> 01:40:12.470
It's a warm community of people who can be vulnerable

2464
01:40:12.470 --> 01:40:15.600
with each other, they've learned how to talk and trust,

2465
01:40:15.600 --> 01:40:17.780
it's an excellent faculty.

2466
01:40:17.780 --> 01:40:21.380
So, this is where the friend they would talk to,

2467
01:40:21.380 --> 01:40:23.370
they're all working in the program.

2468
01:40:23.370 --> 01:40:24.203
Right.

2469
01:40:24.203 --> 01:40:26.690
And the faculty we're all of one mind.

2470
01:40:26.690 --> 01:40:29.463
I mean, we have all different approaches,

2471
01:40:30.330 --> 01:40:33.360
but, I mean, I really believe in this, you know,

2472
01:40:33.360 --> 01:40:35.910
when I look at the transformation that I have seen,

2473
01:40:37.674 --> 01:40:39.490
I'm one part of the thing.

2474
01:40:39.490 --> 01:40:41.340
And I think I have an important part.

2475
01:40:43.350 --> 01:40:44.270
But people get better.

2476
01:40:44.270 --> 01:40:45.197
Mm-hmm.

2477
01:40:45.197 --> 01:40:46.248
And it's an-

2478
01:40:46.248 --> 01:40:47.603
It's beautiful to witness that.

2479
01:40:47.603 --> 01:40:48.436
It's beautiful to witness that.

2480
01:40:48.436 --> 01:40:50.770
And over many years I've seen that unfold

2481
01:40:50.770 --> 01:40:53.530
in lots of different people and it just,

2482
01:40:53.530 --> 01:40:56.012
there's nothing more encouraging or heartwarming

2483
01:40:56.012 --> 01:40:59.020
than seeing that light go on in somebody else

2484
01:40:59.020 --> 01:41:03.290
and then over time watching their life not just change,

2485
01:41:03.290 --> 01:41:04.123
but flourish?

2486
01:41:04.123 --> 01:41:04.956
Mm-hmm.

2487
01:41:04.956 --> 01:41:05.789
It's truly miraculous.

2488
01:41:05.789 --> 01:41:06.622
It really is.

2489
01:41:06.622 --> 01:41:08.620
And so this is a quasi religion,

2490
01:41:08.620 --> 01:41:11.420
which means you have a community, you have a text,

2491
01:41:11.420 --> 01:41:13.880
you have rituals, you have a teaching,

2492
01:41:13.880 --> 01:41:17.347
you have novices moving up through the program, so-

2493
01:41:17.347 --> 01:41:18.460
You got a book too.

2494
01:41:18.460 --> 01:41:19.293
You got a book.

2495
01:41:19.293 --> 01:41:20.323
Yeah.

2496
01:41:20.323 --> 01:41:21.156
You got a Bible.
(Rich laughing)

2497
01:41:21.156 --> 01:41:22.830
Yeah, so, I get it, I get it.

2498
01:41:22.830 --> 01:41:24.369
Yeah.

2499
01:41:24.369 --> 01:41:25.360
I admire it greatly.
Mm-hmm.

2500
01:41:25.360 --> 01:41:30.360
And what I add to it is, the outsider, you know,

2501
01:41:33.730 --> 01:41:36.463
virtue, rationality, wisdom, depth,

2502
01:41:38.010 --> 01:41:40.250
so I have my own take on each of the 12 steps.

2503
01:41:40.250 --> 01:41:42.250
So I said, we're gonna talk about this step today,

2504
01:41:42.250 --> 01:41:44.080
