3028
02:01:08.087 --> 02:01:10.230
And I say, I didn't know who he was, I'm sorry.

3029
02:01:10.230 --> 02:01:11.900
She says, "you sat next to Leonard Cohen?"

3030
02:01:11.900 --> 02:01:13.460
I say, I didn't know.

3031
02:01:13.460 --> 02:01:15.530
So he and Anthony walked into the synagogue

3032
02:01:15.530 --> 02:01:16.380
the next Sabbath.

3033
02:01:17.660 --> 02:01:19.210
And they just start coming to the synagogue

3034
02:01:19.210 --> 02:01:20.870
and attending all my classes,

3035
02:01:20.870 --> 02:01:24.440
and we four became good friends and he and I

3036
02:01:24.440 --> 02:01:27.660
became very connected and I was his rabbi.

3037
02:01:27.660 --> 02:01:28.834
Mm-hmm.

3038
02:01:28.834 --> 02:01:30.223
You know, I can say he was,

3039
02:01:31.700 --> 02:01:35.190
we weren't chummy because we felt a little bit awkward

3040
02:01:35.190 --> 02:01:38.430
around each other, unless we studied something.

3041
02:01:38.430 --> 02:01:40.563
So he really knew Kabbalah very well,

3042
02:01:41.990 --> 02:01:43.690
he clearly has the gift of a muse,

3043
02:01:45.443 --> 02:01:47.520
I got the inner life of his poetry.

3044
02:01:47.520 --> 02:01:48.667
So some time he'd come to me and say he says,

3045
02:01:48.667 --> 02:01:53.040
