I just say, sure.

3047
02:01:54.220 --> 02:01:55.053
You guys, how long you been working on?

3048
02:01:55.053 --> 02:01:55.886
And he says, "15 years."

3049
02:01:55.886 --> 02:01:56.719
Yeah.

3050
02:01:56.719 --> 02:01:57.707
I said, how long"

3051
02:01:57.707 --> 02:01:59.360
He says, "120 verses."

3052
02:01:59.360 --> 02:02:00.193
I said, I got time.

3053
02:02:00.193 --> 02:02:01.320
I was like-
Uh-huh.

3054
02:02:01.320 --> 02:02:02.720
So, you know, and I would say,

3055
02:02:02.720 --> 02:02:04.170
my favorite song is bird on a wire.

3056
02:02:04.170 --> 02:02:05.800
He goes, "oh, you wanna hear the rest of the verses?"

3057
02:02:05.800 --> 02:02:06.633
So, I was like,

3058
02:02:06.633 --> 02:02:09.103
I mean, all of the songs have hundreds of verses, right?

3059
02:02:10.120 --> 02:02:12.903
So we had a great connection, you know,

3060
02:02:13.860 --> 02:02:15.290
I say he wasn't my friend-

3061
02:02:15.290 --> 02:02:16.980
Based on philosophy.

3062
02:02:16.980 --> 02:02:19.673
Philosophy and he wanted a teacher.

3063
02:02:20.800 --> 02:02:24.060
I knew what he wanted because of in the Buddhist world

3064
02:02:24.060 --> 02:02:26.770
where, you know, consciousness gets emptied out,

3065
02:02:26.770 --> 02:02:30.740
and, you know, meditation is a tuning fork to reality,

3066
02:02:30.740 --> 02:02:33.990
he wanted a guy that actually taught moral realism

3067
02:02:34.850 --> 02:02:36.940
and the world is real,

3068
02:02:36.940 --> 02:02:39.963
and there really is a divine interfacing with human beings.

3069
02:02:41.088 --> 02:02:43.410
And it was not what he believed,

3070
02:02:43.410 --> 02:02:45.370
